    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4599" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ausētānus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to the city
				Ausa</i>, <i>in</i> Hispania Tarraconensis: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					29, 2, 2</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ausē-tāni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				Ausetani</i>, Caes B. C. 1, 60; <i><span class="en">Liv. 21,
				23, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">21, 61,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 3, 4, § 22</span></i>; cf. Mann.
			Hispan. p. 404.</div>
